From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ch13726a: name the backlight after the panel's label

The AYN Thor has two panels, each with a DSI backlight named after its
DSI device (ae94000.dsi.0 for this bottom panel, ae96000.dsi.0 for the
top one). Steam's Game Mode brightness slider drives the first entry of
/sys/class/backlight, and ae94000.dsi.0 comes first both alphabetically
and in sysfs order, so the slider dimmed the bottom screen, not the top
one Game Mode runs on.

Name the backlight after the panel node's "label" when it has one. The
Thor's dts labels the bottom panel "bottom-panel", which sorts after
ae96000.dsi.0 both ways, so Steam's slider drives the top panel and the
bottom one keeps a backlight of its own.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ddic-ch13726a.c
@@ -225,8 +225,12 @@
 		.brightness = 255,
 		.max_brightness = 255,
 	};
+	const char *name = dev_name(dev);
 
-	return devm_backlight_device_register(dev, dev_name(dev), dev, dsi,
+	/* the device tree may name the backlight: which panel of several it is */
+	of_property_read_string(dev->of_node, "label", &name);
+
+	return devm_backlight_device_register(dev, name, dev, dsi,
 					      &ch13726a_bl_ops, &props);
 }
 
